    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d223-a5">

                <pb facs="0325" n="251" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg251"/>

                <head>Telegram sent to John A. MacDonald, Esq</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Toronto,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-07-17"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 17, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">John A. MacDonald</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Attorney General, West Ottawa, C. W.:</hi></p>
                <p>Is there any reason why Ellis, Carney, and Dillon, in prison here as Fenians, are
                    not discharged? The evidence of their innocence is conclusive, and the report of
                    Mr. Harrison in favor of their release. I would respectfully ask that they be
                    discharged at once.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>D. THURSTON, <hi rendition="#italic">United States
                    Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
